[76.381092, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m5\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[76.382734, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe graph is a set of six linear components (no branching or cycles), but one non-`F` extension references a missing k-mer. I’ll inspect that boundary and \r\nverify extension consistency correctly before finalizing traversal rules.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\nfrom collections import Counter\r\nrows=[]; d={}\r\nwith open('test') as f:\r\n    for line in f:\r\n        k,e=line.rstrip().split('\\t'); rows.append((k,e[0],e[1])); d[k]=e\r\nkeys=set(d)\r\nedges=[]; bad=[]; inconsistent=[]\r\nfor k,l,r in rows:\r\n    if r!='F':\r\n        nxt=k[1:]+r\r\n        if nxt in keys: edges.append((k,nxt))\r\n        else: bad.append((k,r,nxt))\r\n    if l!='F':\r\n        prv=l+k[:-1]\r\n        if prv not in keys: bad.append((k,l,prv))\r\nfor a,b in edges:\r\n    if d[b][0] != a[0]: inconsistent.append((a,b,d[b][0],a[0]))\r\nprint('bad',bad)\r\nprint('inconsistent',len(inconsistent),inconsistent[:5])\r\n# all non-F edges count\r\nprint('non-F left/right',sum(l!='F' for _,l,r in rows),sum(r!='F' for _,l,r in rows))\r\n# inspect F and nearby path IDs\r\nnextmap={a:b for a,b in edges}; prevmap={b:a for a,b in edges}\r\nstarts=[k for k,l,r in rows if k not in prevmap]\r\nfor i,s in enumerate(starts):\r\n    p=[]; cur=s\r\n    while True:\r\n        p.append(cur)\r\n        if cur not in nextmap: break\r\n        cur=nextmap[cur]\r\n    end=p[-1]\r\n    print(i,'start',s,d[s],'end',end,d[end],'len',len(p))\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
