[94.797618, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m7\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[94.798053, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe data forms linear paths, with a final extension whose next k-mer is absent because the input is truncated at 10,000 lines. I’ll build a general solution \r\nthat: inserts unique k-mers into a chained hash table, derives left/right adjacency from extension characters, and extracts maximal non-branching paths \r\ndeterministically. First I’ll install Berkeley UPC as required.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app\r\nnproc; free -h; df -h /app /tmp | tail -n +2\r\nwhich curl wget make perl python3 g++ || true\r\ncurl -L --fail --max-time 60 -o /tmp/berkeley_upc-2022.10.0.tar.gz https://upc.lbl.gov/download/release/berkeley_upc-2022.10.0.tar.gz && ls -lh \r\n/tmp/berkeley_upc-2022.10.0.tar.gz\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[94.798366, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
