[131.486226, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe configure command exceeded the shell’s 30-second limit. I’ll run installation steps in the background and poll their logs to work around this constraint.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /tmp\r\nls -d berkeley_upc-2022.10.0 2>/dev/null; tail -20 /tmp/upc_configure.log 2>/dev/null; pgrep -af configure || true\r\nif [ ! -f /tmp/upc_configure.done ]; then\r\n  (cd /tmp/berkeley_upc-2022.10.0 && ./configure --prefix=/usr/local --disable-mpi --enable-smp --disable-ibv --disable-shmem --disable-ofi --disable-ucx > \r\n/tmp/upc_configure.log 2>&1; echo $? > /tmp/upc_configure.done) &\r\n  echo \"started configure pid $!\"\r\nfi\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
