[168.962636, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe background configure was terminated with the timed-out shell. I’ll relaunch it detached with `nohup`/`setsid` so it survives across tool invocations, then \r\npoll periodically.\r\n\r\n```\r\nrm -f /tmp/upc_configure.done\r\nnohup setsid bash -c 'cd /tmp/berkeley_upc-2022.10.0 && ./configure --prefix=/usr/local --disable-mpi --enable-smp --disable-ibv --disable-shmem --disable-ofi \r\n--disable-ucx > /tmp/upc_configure.log 2>&1; echo $? > /tmp/upc_configure.done' </dev/null >/tmp/upc_launch.log 2>&1 &\r\necho \"launched configure pid $!\"\r\nsleep 2\r\nps -eo pid,ppid,stat,etime,cmd | grep -E '[c]onfigure' | head -3\r\ntail -3 /tmp/upc_configure.log\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
