[331.627612, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m20\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[331.628107, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe default compiler network is UDP; I need to select the SMP conduit explicitly at compile time. I’ll rebuild the test with `-network=smp` and run it with four\r\nthreads.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -x\r\n/usr/local/opt/bin/upcc -network=smp -o /tmp/hello_smp /tmp/hello.upc && echo COMPILED\r\n/usr/local/bin/upcrun -n 4 -shared-heap 256MB /tmp/hello_smp\r\necho rc=$?\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[331.628364, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[333.966811, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[333.967112, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n+ /usr/local/opt/bin/upcc -network=smp -o /tmp/hello_smp /tmp/hello.upc\r\n+ echo COMPILED\r\nCOMPILED\r\n+ /usr/local/bin/upcrun -n 4 -shared-heap 256MB /tmp/hello_smp\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 2 of 4 on 20583e9ac8c2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 2 of 4, pid=46557)\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 0 of 4 on 20583e9ac8c2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 0 of 4, pid=46538)\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 1 of 4 on 20583e9ac8c2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 1 of 4, pid=46556)\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 3 of 4 on 20583e9ac8c2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 3 of 4, pid=46558)\r\nUPC Runtime warning: Requested shared memory (256 MB) > available (9 MB) on node 0 (20583e9ac8c2): using 9 MB per thread instead\r\nT0 a[0]=0\r\nT0 a[4]=16\r\nT2 a[2]=4\r\nT3 a[3]=9\r\nT1 a[1]=1\r\n+ echo rc=0\r\nrc=0\r\n\r\n"]
