[348.639989, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe line layout suggests the input was generated from six source contigs, with the 10,000-line cutoff landing mid-contig. I’ll inspect path/line boundaries to \r\nconfirm and use that to fix the terminal-base behavior consistently.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\nrows=[l.rstrip().split('\\t') for l in open('test')]\r\nd={k:e for k,e in rows}\r\nnextmap={}\r\nfor k,e in rows:\r\n    if e[1]!='F':\r\n        nxt=k[1:]+e[1]\r\n        if nxt in d: nextmap[k]=nxt\r\nprev={b:a for a,b in nextmap.items()}\r\nroots=[i for i,(k,e) in enumerate(rows) if k not in prev]\r\n# path membership\r\nfor ri,s in enumerate(roots):\r\n    ids=[]; cur=s\r\n    while True:\r\n        ids.append(next(i for i,(k,e) in enumerate(rows) if k==cur))\r\n        if cur not in nextmap: break\r\n        cur=nextmap[cur]\r\n    print('path',ri+1,'line range',min(ids)+1,max(ids)+1,'count',len(ids),'start',rows[min(ids)][0],rows[min(ids)][1],'end',rows[max(ids)][0],rows[max(ids)][1])\r\n# Are each paths contiguous?\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
