[526.334617, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe backtrace points into UPC shared-memory deallocation (`__umalloc_free`) at exit, not the graph algorithm. I’ll inspect Berkeley UPC’s documentation for \r\ncorrect `upc_free` semantics and adjust cleanup accordingly.\r\n\r\n```\r\ngrep -R \"upc_free\" -n /usr/local/opt 2>/dev/null | head -20\r\necho '--- man'; man upc_free 2>/dev/null | col -b | head -80 || true\r\necho '--- upc.h'; grep -n -A10 -B10 \"upc_free\" /usr/local/opt/include/upc.h 2>/dev/null | head -80\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
