[590.746155, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m39\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[590.746552, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe pure-cycle edge case produced an extra rotation (`ACGTAC` instead of `ACGT`), even though serial and UPC agree. I’ll inspect the cycle traversal logic and \r\nhash lookup to fix the cycle termination correctly.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app\r\necho 'file:'; cat -A /tmp/edge/cycle\r\nrm -f /app/serial.out; ./serial /tmp/edge/cycle\r\necho 'serial length:'; awk '{print length($0),$0}' /app/serial.out\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\nrows=[]\r\nfor l in open('/tmp/edge/cycle'):\r\n    k,e=l.rstrip('\\n').split('\\t'); rows.append((k,e[0],e[1]))\r\nd={k:e for k,e in rows}; k=len(rows[0][0])\r\nnextmap={}\r\nfor km,l,r in rows:\r\n    if r!='F':\r\n        nxt=km[1:]+r\r\n        nextmap[km]=nxt if nxt in d else None\r\nprint(rows,nextmap)\r\n# trace\r\nstart=rows[0][0]; cur=start; seq=start\r\nfor step in range(10):\r\n    nxt=nextmap.get(cur)\r\n    print(step,cur,'right',d[cur][1],'next',nxt)\r\n    if nxt is None or nxt==start: break\r\n    seq += d[cur][1]\r\n    cur=nxt\r\nprint('seq',seq)\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[590.746952, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[590.763645, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[590.763836, "o", "<returncode>\r\n1\r\n<output>\r\nfile:\r\nACG^ITT$\r\nCGT^IAA$\r\nGTA^ICC$\r\nTAC^IGG$\r\nserial length:\r\n6 ACGTAC\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 4, in <module>\r\nValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 2)\r\n\r\n"]
